        {
          "id": "about-section-2",
          "type": "story_block",
          "intent": "Tell the founding story and editorial philosophy in a way that differentiates Pixelwave from legacy tech media and builds emotional connection.",
          "eyebrow": "Our Story",
          "headline": "Born in the Browser, Built for the Next Era",
          "subheadline": null,
          "body": "Pixelwave launched in 2021 because we were tired of technology journalism that either fawned over founders or reduced every breakthrough to a bullet-point explainer. The future is complicated, contested, and genuinely exciting \u2014 and it deserved a publication willing to sit with that complexity.\n\nWe are a small, independent team of journalists, technologists, and obsessives who believe that the best technology writing is also great writing. We do not accept sponsored content. We do not write press releases in disguise. Every story we publish has been reported, argued over, edited, and re-edited until it earns its place.\n\nOur editorial philosophy is simple: respect the reader's intelligence, take the technology seriously, and never mistake hype for substance. The future is buffering \u2014 and we are here to help you read the signal through the noise.",
